<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 42,677 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 42,677 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 42,677 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 40,021 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Wednesday   Sept 24</p>
<p>    Export cargo			   5,772	2,075</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  36,905     37,946</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, 15 were expected to arrive and three were expected to sail.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     30,445	 Pandelis - L	 26/9</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     30,551	 Yenisei		26/9</p>
<p>Chemicals		 7,690	 Bow Fagus	    26/9</p>
<p>Containers		  600	 Song Shan	    26/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
